Third-party code vendored into impromptu
========================================

impromptu is MIT (see ../../../LICENSE). The files in this directory are
third-party MIT code, kept here with their attribution rather than rewritten.


speech-matcher.js
-----------------
Ported from:  https://github.com/jlecomte/voice-activated-teleprompter
License:      MIT
Copyright:    (c) 2024 - Present, Julien Lecomte - All Rights Reserved

Contains ports of `src/lib/speech-matcher.ts`, `src/lib/word-tokenizer.ts`, and
`src/lib/levenshtein.ts`.

`levenshtein.ts` is itself vendored by that project from:
  https://github.com/gustf/js-levenshtein  (MIT, (c) Gustaf Andersson)

Why vendored rather than depended on: the upstream project is a React + Redux +
Vite single-page application, and impromptu's web UI is deliberately plain ES
modules with no bundler and no npm. Only the three pure functions are needed,
so they were ported and the application layer was left behind.

Changes made in the port:
  - TypeScript to plain ES modules; types expressed as JSDoc
  - identifiers renamed to camelCase house style
  - comments added explaining the windowing behaviour
  - an unclosed `[` hint now stays a single delimiter instead of consuming the
    remainder of the script

The matching algorithm is unchanged. Behaviour is pinned by
tests/test_speech_matcher.mjs.


